Conduct targeted research, quantitative and qualitative analyses to inform policy, regulatory and investment decision in the space domain&nbsp;






Develop and maintain structured databases and analyse datasets (expetced) and build simple quantitative and economic models (a strong plus) to support consulting assignments.&nbsp;&nbsp;






Produce high-quality, client-ready deliverables (presentations, reports, strategic recommendations), translating complex analyses into clear, actionable insights&nbsp;






Lead and participate to proposal development and business development activities, including shaping value propositions and supporting tender responses&nbsp;






Fluency in English (additional language is a plus)&nbsp;



Experience & Education 



Up to 4 years of relevant professional experience (consulting, public sector advisory, or space-related roles)&nbsp;






Strong academic background with a Master’s degree in a relevant field (e.g., space studies, engineering, economics, public policy, international relations, or equivalent)&nbsp;






Knowledge of econometric methods and modelling is a strong asset.&nbsp;



Required Skills 



Strong analytical skills&nbsp;






Excellent PowerPoint, Excel and written/oral communication skills&nbsp;






Proven ability for research, synthesis, and structuring complex information&nbsp;






Demonstrated interest or knowledge in the space sector&nbsp;



We offer



Growth opportunities in a dynamic team with an outstanding network of sector experts&nbsp;






Direct project interaction and mentoring by our partners who have extensive background in international management consulting&nbsp;






Work in the most inspiring of industries with impact in the space industry&nbsp;






Development of your management consultancy skill set&nbsp;






International work environment &nbsp;






Intellectual challenges paired with work-life balance and limited travel&nbsp;



Benefits



Bonus based on performance&nbsp;






Profit-sharing bonus&nbsp;






Meal voucher : 12 € / working day (50% by employer)&nbsp;






Remote work : 2 days/week&nbsp;



