ABOUT US
&nbsp;
Unzer is a leading European fintech company with a mission to simplify international payments for e-commerce and retail businesses. Our brand was formed from 13 companies that now contribute to building a unique product covering the entire payment flow.&nbsp;&nbsp;
&nbsp;
At Unzer, we are driven by the belief that customers should enjoy a seamless shopping experience, no matter where they choose to shop. We are a team of over 700 experts of 55 different nationalities, dedicated to creating a state-of-the-art unified commerce platform. Our goal is to enable businesses to delight their customers with a seamless payment experience.&nbsp;&nbsp;
&nbsp;
Whether you're a tech enthusiast, payment expert, or a dedicated support professional, we are looking for individuals who are passionate about making a difference.&nbsp;&nbsp;
&nbsp;
Our offices: We are based across Austria, Denmark, Germany and Luxembourg with a HQ in Berlin.
&nbsp;
ABOUT THE TEAM
Unzer's POS department is the commercial engine connecting Unzer's terminal technology to merchants across Europe — spanning Field &amp; Inside Sales, Merchant Services, Onboarding, Technical Support, and Sales Strategy. As Product Manager for traditional POS, you'll own the commercial and operational product experience around our point-of-sale payment terminal business. You'll work at the intersection of external vendors, Sales, Key Account Management, Onboarding, and Strategy to turn field insights into product and process improvements that make a real difference to merchants, vendors, and to the teams who support them.&nbsp;
What your work will look like:

Own the Product Roadmap &amp; its Delivery:&nbsp;Build and execute the product roadmap for one or more product areas, ensuring on-time delivery of features and improvements that support business objectives.&nbsp;
Business Impact &amp; Prioritization Ownership:&nbsp;Co-own prioritization and business impact of product initiatives, focusing on revenue growth and cost efficiency.&nbsp;
KPI Definition &amp; Performance Tracking:&nbsp;Define and track KPIs across multiple product areas to measure product success and drive continuous improvement in alignment with Unzer’s strategic goals.&nbsp;
Drive Cross-functional Initiatives:&nbsp;Lead cross-team collaboration by influencing critical operational decisions, managing resources, and facilitating effective execution of major product initiatives.&nbsp;
Facilitate collaboration:&nbsp;Build effective relationships with internal colleagues and external partners to gather requirements, communicate priorities, and ensure successful project outcomes.&nbsp;
Resource Allocation and Performance Management:&nbsp;Oversee allocation and effective use of resources within your domain, monitoring project progress, mitigating risks, and driving performance to meet technical and group objectives.&nbsp;

What you need to be successful in this role:

5+ years product management experience in Tech, ideally in Payments Hardware - a plus if gained within a financially regulated company.&nbsp;
You have robust experience planning and executing product initiatives while establishing milestones to ensure on-time, on-budget, and high-quality delivery.&nbsp;
You are data driven and solving complex problems by identifying the best path to deliver value faster comes naturally to you.&nbsp;
You facilitate cross-functional collaboration between teams and build strong relationships with diverse internal and external stakeholders.&nbsp;
You communicate with impact, clearly conveying complex ideas to varied audiences, leading discussions, building consensus, and influencing key decisions.&nbsp;
You bring creativity and a continuous improvement mindset, delivering innovative solutions and leading product or process enhancements.&nbsp;
You demonstrate leadership and adaptability by guiding teams through change, embracing new technologies and AI practices, and maintaining high professional standards.&nbsp;
Fluent in German and English

Please note that we will not sponsor your visa or relocation, and you must have a valid work permit to be eligible for this position.&nbsp;
What’s next? 

Does it sound exciting? -&nbsp; Apply with your CV in English. Please don’t shy away if you don’t meet all the requirements! We’re looking forward to meeting you.&nbsp;&nbsp;
The interview process includes: a 30min intro call with a TA Partner, a 60-min Hiring Manager interview, a 45-min skills assessment call with a stakeholder and a final executive interview, 30 min. Please note the process might alter depending on our team’s availability.&nbsp;




WHAT WE OFFER&nbsp;


More than a workplace. A place to grow. 🌍&nbsp;


At Unzer, colleagues from 50+ nationalities across four countries work together to create better outcomes for our merchants. We take ownership, move with pace and keep raising the bar—as one team.&nbsp;


We set high expectations and give you the flexibility, learning opportunities and practical support to do your best work, grow your impact, and build a sustainable career.&nbsp;


🏡 Flexibility that works&nbsp;Combine focused time at home with connection and collaboration in the office. Our hybrid setup includes two office days per week.&nbsp;


🚲 Your commute, your choice&nbsp;Choose the mobility benefit that works for you: bike leasing or a Deutschlandticket. &nbsp;


🏖️ Work from anywhere in the EU&nbsp;Change your perspective and work from another EU country for up to 15 days per year.&nbsp;


📗 Keep raising the bar&nbsp;Use an annual learning budget of €1,000 for courses, conferences, certifications and other development opportunities that help you grow and increase your impact. &nbsp;


🫴 Support when you need it&nbsp;Access confidential counselling whenever you need support with personal or professional matters.&nbsp;


💰 Build your future&nbsp;Look ahead with our company pension scheme and take care of your long-term financial wellbeing.&nbsp;
&nbsp;


Benefits may vary by location and employment setup. Your recruiter will share the details relevant to your role.&nbsp;

&nbsp;

